Decision: A successful DAV PUT without If-Match is blind, including any successful short-write attempt without If-Match. Preserve Blind if a later retry uses an ETag. Use only the successful PUT response's versionOf, including Last-Modified when its Date is at least one second later; do not carry forward the old read's timestamp. HTTP dates are not write preconditions and do not provide lost-update protection. Correctness assumes a server enforces If-Match. Blind reconciliation restores the previous merge baseline after another writer overwrites this write; a writer whose change was overwritten must sync again. A cached, identifiable truncated copy remains eligible for existing damage recovery.

